[Applause]  see a sports coverage to the NFL brings  us to Gillette Stadium in Foxborough  mass a moment ago the defending Super  Bowl champs introduced to this fired up  crowd here in Foxborough as the Patriots  get set to do battle with mat Lyon and  the defending NFC champions the Atlanta  Falcons hey everyone its Peter Brown  standing in for Alex Newhouse for his  review of Madden 18  although Madden releases feature a  little more than mechanical tweaks and  roster updates Madden NFL 18 is  highlighted by one of the most  significant additions in the series  history a full story mode and this is on  top of a much more graphically capable  engine as well as a result Madden 18 is  a distinct improvement over the last  several entries in the series  [Applause]  touchdown  [Applause]  Madden games rarely tackled a personal  side of football choosing instead to  present it as a chess like competition  you are the coach and master the players  are your instruments to score of course  that's not how football is treated in  the real world so to see that change in  Madden is intriguing in theory and  gratifying in practice the longshot  story mode actually references the deep  emotional investment people have in the  sport and how high the stakes are for  them for example main character Devon  Wade the star football player from his  small Texas town quits his college team  after a family tragedy you navigate  through Wade's attempt to return to  football traveling to the NFL Combine in  order to impress Scouts longshot is  surprisingly deep it's a fully fledged  telltale style adventure game with  multiple endings broken up by short  moments of actually playing football it  presents you with decisions that affect  both the people around you and the  scouts perception of you as with  telltale games there's an illusion of  greater choice that isn't necessarily  there but longshots succeeds because it  makes minor choices feel important I'll  pass I'm a football player not an actor  Oh football player huh what team do you  play for the mode is at its best when  his characters speak honestly about  their love for the sport nailing the  sense that football offers something  bigger a connection to a community and a  way to achieve greatness it has issues  with over-the-top spectacle but on the  whole this first attempt at a story mode  from Madden creates an excellent  foundation for the series further once  you finish long shot you can dive into  madden ultimate team to play through  Devon Wade's most memorable football  scenarios has been impressive so far in  relief of caleb young bringing the  bullfrogs back from a huge deficit  freak around and win this game madden  ultimate team is undoubtedly Madden's  deepest mode which has received a suite  of updates to make it even more  appealing to returning players you'll  get player cards representing Devon Wade  Colt Cruz and other characters from long  shot and forming a long shot focused  mutt team lets you participate in around  30 challenges although these challenges  are generally not much more than normal  Madden scenarios with longshot player  models they're still entertaining enough  to be worth playing on the field Madden  a team looks beautiful the game is the  first in the series to use EA's  frostbite engine and as a result certain  moments look nearly photorealistic  stadiums feature minor details while  player models show everything from arm  tattoos to jersey wrinkles Stadium  lighting is a particular high point for  example afternoon sunlight partially  blocked by the stadium edges filters  down on the parts of the field and  realistically illuminates players as  they run into the light the transition  to frostbite isn't perfect though  outside of stadium's environments  generally look bland and featureless  especially during segments of long shot  additionally with more human-like player  movements come some bizarre graphical  bugs such as a player's leg clipping  through his tacklers chest where two  players getting hung up on each other as  they try to stand up as with past Madden  games EA is trying to make sure that the  game reflects real NFL events as much as  possible which means weekly roster and  player stat updates this year EA has  also added the play now live mode which  allows you to jump quickly into any of  this week's matchups and both teams will  reflect the actual lineups set to play  EA Tiburon has also introduced the  ability to turn play now live games into  a franchise letting you jump into a full  season immediately after completing the  game even though franchise mode hasn't  received many updates from last year's  version these new starting points make  it a whole lot easier and more enticing  to play through an entire season  [Applause]  sixteen touchdown  [Applause]  overall Madden 18 marks an unusually  large shake-up in a series that due to  its annualized releases rarely features  more than small iterative changes the  Frostbite engine allows the game to  achieve new levels of realism in its  visuals an EA has put a lot of effort  into constantly evolving the game to  keep it in line with real world events  but it is the longshots story mode that  defines Madden 18 some of longshot is  unnecessary spectacle but it's lasting  value comes from the humanity that it  brings to the game these moments of  vulnerability and sincerity between  Devon Wade and Colt Cruz during the  story are worthy of celebration and give  the overall game a weight that madden  hasn't had before and if that's not  enough to entice you it's also simply a  terrific football game  [Music]  you  [Music]

